  "releaseNotes": "11.0.0\n\n* New: a net11.0 build, for .NET 11. The netstandard2.0, net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 builds stay,\n  so nothing changes for a project on an earlier .NET.\n* The major version is 11 because it follows the .NET generation, as 10.0.0 did for .NET 10. No\n  API was added, changed or removed since 10.3.4: code that builds against 10.3.4 builds against\n  11.0.0 as it is.\n* On netstandard2.0 only (which is what .NET Framework uses), the System.Text.Json and\n  Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces dependencies move from 10.0.13 to 11.0.0, in step with\n  Com.H.Data.Common 11.0.0. The other builds still have no dependencies.\n\nUpgrading from before 10.3.4? 10.3.4 changed the type GetDataModelParameters gives a JSON integer\nfrom 2^53 on, 10.3.3 how Fill and FillDate treat a value that holds a placeholder, 10.3.1 what\nIOExtensions.UnifyPathSeperator does with a leading // or \\\\ on Windows, and 10.3.0 how Com.H.Shell\nand Com.H.Pdf behave. The notes of 10.3.0 to 10.3.4 list every change:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.4#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.3#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.2#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.1#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.0#releasenotes-body-tab",
